      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[6]_{9}?$\n\n- $-12$\n- $3$\n- $24$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue class $[6]_{9}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $6$ modulo $9.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[6]_{9} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=6+9k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={6+9k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,6-2\\cdot 9,\\,6-9,\\,6,\\,6+9,\\,6+2\\cdot 9,\\,…} \\\\  & ={…,-12,-3,6,15,24,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-12$ and $24$ belong to $[6]_{9},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
